Package: natmcp
Type: Package
Title: MCP Server Providing Grounded natverse Knowledge to Coding Agents
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Gregory", "Jefferis", email = "jefferis@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0587-9355"))
Description: An MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that gives coding agents
    authoritative, current, token-efficient access to natverse ground truth so
    they can generate, extend, optimise and repurpose natverse analysis code
    efficiently. It builds a live index by introspecting installed natverse
    packages (namespaces, formals, Rd, executed examples) and harvesting
    machine-readable artefacts (pkgdown reference groups, vignettes, examples),
    augmented by a small curated corpus (a package/altitude guide, a dataset
    facts table, task-oriented snippets). The index backs six lean tools:
    guide, find, signature, snippet, dataset and lint. Built on 'mcptools'
    (transport) and 'ellmer' (typed tools), delegating generic package
    documentation to 'btw' and adding the curated natverse knowledge layer on
    top; the tools compose with 'btw' in a single server.
